H6900.definition:
or קְבֻרָה; feminine passive participle of H6912 (קָבַר);
sepulture; (concretely) a sepulchre
KJV: burial, burying place, grave, sepulchre.

H6901.definition:
a primitive root;
to admit, i.e. take (literally or figuratively)
KJV: choose, (take) hold, receive, (under-) take.

H6902.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6901 (קָבַל);
to acquire
KJV: receive, take.

H6903.definition:
(Aramaic) or קֳבֵל; (Aramaic), (corresponding to H6905 (קָבָל);
(adverbially) in front of; usually (with other particles) on account of, so as, since, hence
KJV: [phrase] according to, [phrase] as, [phrase] because, before, [phrase] for this cause, [phrase] forasmuch as, [phrase] by this means, over against, by reason of, [phrase] that, [phrase] therefore, [phrase] though, [phrase] wherefore.

H6904.definition:
from H6901 (קָבַל) in the sense of confronting (as standing opposite in order to receive);
a battering-ram
KJV: war.

H6905.definition:
from H6901 (קָבַל) in the sense of opposite (see H6904 (קֹבֶל));
the presence, i.e. (adverbially) in front of
KJV: before.

H6906.definition:
a primitive root;
to cover, i.e. (figuratively) defraud
KJV: rob, spoil.

H6907.definition:
from H6906 (קָבַע);
a goblet (as deep like a cover)
KJV: dregs.

H6908.definition:
a primitive root;
to grasp, i.e. collect
KJV: assemble (selves), gather (bring) (together, selves together, up), heap, resort, [idiom] surely, take up.

H6909.definition:
from H6908 (קָבַץ) and H410 (אֵל); God has gathered;
Kabtseel, a place in Palestine
KJV: Kabzeel. Compare H3343 (יְקַבְצְאֵל).

H6910.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6908 (קָבַץ);
a hoard
KJV: [idiom] gather.

H6911.definition:
dual from H6908 (קָבַץ); a double heap;
Kibtsajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Kibzaim.

H6912.definition:
a primitive root;
to inter
KJV: [idiom] in any wise, bury(-ier).

H6913.definition:
or (feminine) קִבְרָה; from H6912 (קָבַר);
a sepulchre
KJV: burying place, grave, sepulchre.

H6914.definition:
from the feminine plural of H6913 (קֶבֶר) and H8378 (תַּאֲוָה) with the article interposed; graves of the longing;
Kibroth-hat-Taavh, a place in the Desert
KJV: Kibroth-hattaavah.

H6915.definition:
a primitive root;
to shrivel up, i.e. contract or bend the body (or neck) in deference
KJV: bow (down) (the) head, stoop.

H6916.definition:
from H6915 (קָדַד);
cassia bark (as in shrivelled rolls)
KJV: cassia.

H6917.definition:
passive participle of H6923 (קָדַם);
a pristine hero
KJV: ancient.

H6918.definition:
or קָדֹשׁ; from H6942 (קָדַשׁ);
sacred (ceremonially or morally); (as noun) God (by eminence), an angel, a saint, a sanctuary
KJV: holy (One), saint.

H6920.definition:
from H6919 (קָדַח);
inflammation, i.e. febrile disease
KJV: burning ague, fever.

H6921.definition:
or קָדִם; from H6923 (קָדַם);
the fore or front part; hence (by orientation) the East (often adverbially, eastward, for brevity the east wind)
KJV: east(-ward, wind).

H6922.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6918 (קָדוֹשׁ).
{sacred (ceremonially or morally); (as noun) God (by eminence), an angel, a saint, a sanctuary}
KJV: holy (One), saint.

H6923.definition:
a primitive root;
to project (one self), i.e. precede; hence, to anticipate, hasten, meet (usually for help)
KJV: come (go, (flee)) before, [phrase] disappoint, meet, prevent.

H6924.definition:
or קֵדְמָה; from H6923 (קָדַם);
the front, of place (absolutely, the fore part, relatively the East) or time (antiquity); often used adverbially (before, anciently, eastward)
KJV: aforetime, ancient (time), before, east (end, part, side, -ward), eternal, [idiom] ever(-lasting), forward, old, past. Compare H6926 (קִדְמָה).

H6925.definition:
(Aramaic) or קְדָם; (Aramaic) (Daniel 7:13), corresponding to H6924 (קֶדֶם);
before
KJV: before, [idiom] from, [idiom] I (thought), [idiom] me, [phrase] of, [idiom] it pleased, presence.

H6926.definition:
feminine of H6924 (קֶדֶם);
the forward part (or relatively) East (often adverbially, on the east or in front)
KJV: east(-ward).

H6927.definition:
from H6923 (קָדַם);
priority (in time); also used adverbially (before)
KJV: afore, antiquity, former (old) estate.

H6928.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6927 (קַדְמָה);
former time
KJV: afore(-time), ago.

H6929.definition:
from H6923 (קָדַם); precedence;
Kedemah, a son of Ishmael
KJV: Kedemah.

H6931.definition:
or קַדְמֹנִי; from H6930 (קַדְמוֹן);
(of time) anterior or (of place) oriental
KJV: ancient, they that went before, east, (thing of) old.

H6932.definition:
from H6923 (קָדַם); beginnings;
Kedemoth, a place in eastern Palestine
KJV: Kedemoth.

H6933.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H6923 (קָדַם);
first
KJV: first.

H6934.definition:
from H6924 (קֶדֶם) and H410 (אֵל); presence of God;
Kadmiel, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Kadmiel.

H6935.definition:
the same as H6931 (קַדְמוֹנִי); ancient, i.e. aboriginal;
Kadmonite (collectively), the name of a tribe in Palestine
KJV: Kadmonites.

H6936.definition:
from H6915 (קָדַד);
the crown of the head (as the part most bowed)
KJV: crown (of the head), pate, scalp, top of the head.

H6937.definition:
a primitive root;
to be ashy, i.e. darkcolored; by implication, to mourn (in sackcloth or sordid garments)
KJV: be black(-ish), be (make) dark(-en), [idiom] heavily, (cause to) mourn.

H6938.definition:
from H6937 (קָדַר); dusky (of the skin or the tent);
Kedar, a son of Ishmael; also (collectively) Bedouin (as his descendants or representatives)
KJV: Kedar.

H6939.definition:
from H6937 (קָדַר); dusky place;
Kidron, a brook near Jerusalem
KJV: Kidron.

H6941.definition:
adverb from H6937 (קָדַר);
blackish ones (i.e. in sackcloth); used adverbially, in mourning weeds
KJV: mournfully.

H6942.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make, pronounce or observe as) clean (ceremonially or morally)
KJV: appoint, bid, consecrate, dedicate, defile, hallow, (be, keep) holy(-er, place), keep, prepare, proclaim, purify, sanctify(-ied one, self), [idiom] wholly.

H6943.definition:
from H6942 (קָדַשׁ); a sanctum;
Kedesh, the name of four places in Palestine
KJV: Kedesh.

H6944.definition:
from H6942 (קָדַשׁ);
a sacred place or thing; rarely abstract, sanctity
KJV: consecrated (thing), dedicated (thing), hallowed (thing), holiness, ([idiom] most) holy ([idiom] day, portion, thing), saint, sanctuary.

H6945.definition:
from H6942 (קָדַשׁ);
a (quasi) sacred person, i.e. (technically) a (male) devotee (by prostitution) to licentious idolatry
KJV: sodomite, unclean.

H6946.definition:
the same as H6945 (קָדֵשׁ); sanctuary;
Kadesh, a place in the Desert
KJV: Kadesh. Compare H6947 (קָדֵשׁ בַּרְנֵעַ).

H6947.definition:
from the same as H6946 (קָדֵשׁ) and an otherwise unused word (apparently compounded of a correspondent to H1251 (בַּר) and a derivative of H5128 (נוּעַ)) meaning desert of a fugitive; Kadesh of (the) Wilderness of Wandering;
Kadesh-Barnea, a place in the Desert
KJV: Kadeshbarnea.

H6948.definition:
feminine of H6945 (קָדֵשׁ);
a female devotee (i.e. prostitute)
KJV: harlot, whore.

H6949.definition:
a primitive root;
to be dull
KJV: be set on edge, be blunt.

H6950.definition:
a primitive root;
to convoke
KJV: assemble (selves) (together), gather (selves) (together).

H6951.definition:
from H6950 (קָהַל);
assemblage (usually concretely)
KJV: assembly, company, congregation, multitude.

H6952.definition:
from H6950 (קָהַל);
an assemblage
KJV: assembly, congregation.

H6953.definition:
feminine of active participle from H6950 (קָהַל);
a (female) assembler (i.e. lecturer); abstractly, preaching (used as a 'nom de plume', Koheleth)
KJV: preacher.

H6954.definition:
from H6950 (קָהַל); convocation;
Kehelathah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Kehelathah.

H6955.definition:
from an unused root meaning to ally oneself; allied;
Kehath, an Israelite
KJV: Kohath.

H6956.definition:
patronymically from H6955 (קְהָת);
a Kohathite (collectively) or descendants of Kehath
KJV: Kohathites.

H6957.definition:
or קָו; from H6960 (קָוָה) (compare H6961 (קָוֶה));
a cord (as connecting), especially formeasuring; figuratively, a rule; also a rim, a musical string or accord
KJV: line. Compare H6978 (קַו־קַו)lemma קַו־קַי yod, corrected to קַו־קַו.

H6958.definition:
or קָיָה; (Jeremiah 25:27), a primitive root;
to vomit
KJV: spue (out), vomit (out, up, up again).

H6959.definition:
a form collateral to H3553 (כּוֹבַע);
a helmet
KJV: helmet.

H6960.definition:
a primitive root;
to bind together (perhaps by twisting), i.e. collect; (figuratively) to expect
KJV: gather (together), look, patiently, tarry, wait (for, on, upon).

H6961.definition:
from H6960 (קָוָה);
a (measuring) cord (as if for binding)
KJV: line.

H6962.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cut off, i.e. (figuratively) detest
KJV: begrieved, loathe self.

H6963.definition:
or קֹל; from an unused root meaning to call aloud;
a voice or sound
KJV: [phrase] aloud, bleating, crackling, cry ([phrase] out), fame, lightness, lowing, noise, [phrase] hold peace, (pro-) claim, proclamation, [phrase] sing, sound, [phrase] spark, thunder(-ing), voice, [phrase] yell.

H6964.definition:
from H6963 (קוֹל) and H3050 (יָהּ); voice of Jah;
Kolajah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Kolaiah.

H6965.definition:
a primitive root;
to rise (in various applications, literal, figurative, intensive and causative)
KJV: abide, accomplish, [idiom] be clearer, confirm, continue, decree, [idiom] be dim, endure, [idiom] enemy, enjoin, get up, make good, help, hold, (help to) lift up (again), make, [idiom] but newly, ordain, perform, pitch, raise (up), rear (up), remain, (a-) rise (up) (again, against), rouse up, set (up), (e-) stablish, (make to) stand (up), stir up, strengthen, succeed, (as-, make) sure(-ly), (be) up(-hold, -rising).

H6966.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6965 (קוּם)
{to rise (in various applications, literal, figurative, intensive and causative)}
KJV: appoint, establish, make, raise up self, (a-) rise (up), (make to) stand, set (up).

H6967.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם);
height
KJV: [idiom] along, height, high, stature, tall.

H6968.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם);
elevation, i.e. (adverbially) erectly (figuratively)
KJV: upright.

H6969.definition:
a primitive root;
to strike a musical note, i.e. chant or wail (at a funeral)
KJV: lament, mourning woman.

H6970.definition:
probably from H6972 (קוּץ) in the original sense of cutting off; curtailment;
Koa, a region of Babylon
KJV: Koa.

H6972.definition:
a primitive root; to clip off; used only as denominative from H7019 (קַיִץ);
to spend the harvest season
KJV: summer.

H6973.definition:
a primitive root (identical with through the idea of severing oneself from (compare H6962 (קוּט)));
to be (causatively, make) disgusted or anxious
KJV: abhor, be distressed, be grieved, loathe, vex, be weary.

H6974.definition:
a primitive root (identical with through the idea of abruptness in starting up from sleep (compare H3364 (יָקַץ)));
to awake (literally or figuratively)
KJV: arise, (be) (a-) wake, watch.

H6975.definition:
or קֹץ; from H6972 (קוּץ) (in the sense of pricking);
a thorn
KJV: thorn.

H6976.definition:
the same as H6975 (קוֹץ);
Kots, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Koz, Hakkoz (including the article).

H6977.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6972 (קוּץ) in its original sense;
a forelock (as shorn)
KJV: lock.

H6978.definition:
from H6957 (קַו) (in the sense of a fastening);
stalwart
KJV: [idiom] meted out.

H6980.definition:
from H6979 (קוּר);
(only plural) trenches, i.e. a web (as if so formed)
KJV: web.

H6981.definition:
or קֹרֵא; (1 Chronicles 26:1), active participle of H7121 (קָרָא); crier;
Kore, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Kore.

H6982.definition:
or קֹרָה; from H6979 (קוּר);
a rafter (forming trenches as it were); by implication, a roof
KJV: beam, roof.

H6984.definition:
from the passive participle of H6983 (קוֹשׁ) and H3050 (יָהּ); entrapped of Jah;
Kushajah, an Israelite
KJV: Kushaiah.

H6985.definition:
from H6990 (קָטַט) in the sense of abbreviation;
a little, i.e. (adverbially) merely
KJV: very.

H6986.definition:
from an unused root meaning to cut off;
ruin
KJV: destroying, destruction.

H6987.definition:
from the same as H6986 (קֶטֶב);
extermination
KJV: destruction.

H6989.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6999 (קָטַר); perfumed;
Keturah, a wife of Abraham
KJV: Keturah.

H6990.definition:
a primitive root;
to clip off, i.e. (figuratively) destroy
KJV: be cut off.

H6991.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cut off, i.e. (figuratively) put to death
KJV: kill, slay.

H6992.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6991 (קָטַל);
to kill
KJV: slay.

H6993.definition:
from H6991 (קָטַל);
a violent death
KJV: slaughter.

H6994.definition:
a primitive root (rather denominative from H6996 (קָטָן));
to diminish, i.e. be (causatively, make) diminutive or (figuratively) of no account
KJV: be a (make) small (thing), be not worthy.

H6995.definition:
from H6994 (קָטֹן);
a pettiness, i.e. the little finger
KJV: little finger.

H6996.definition:
or קָטֹן; from H6962 (קוּט);
abbreviated, i.e. diminutive, literally (in quantity, size or number) or figuratively (in age or importance)
KJV: least, less(-er), little (one), small(-est, one, quantity, thing), young(-er, -est).

H6997.definition:
the same as H6996 (קָטָן); small;
Katan, an Israelite
KJV: Hakkatan (including the article).

H6998.definition:
a primitive root;
to strip off
KJV: crop off, cut down (up), pluck.

H6999.definition:
a primitive root (identical with through the idea of fumigation in a close place and perhaps thus driving out the occupants);
to smoke, i.e. turn into fragrance by fire (especially as an act of worship)
KJV: burn (incense, sacrifice) (upon), (altar for) incense, kindle, offer (incense, a sacrifice).
